# tab_quickstart.sh configuration
#
# Copy to <repo-root>/tab_quickstart.conf (gitignored by default) and edit
# values for your environment.
#
# Config file resolution priority (high to low):
#   1. $TAB_CONFIG env var (explicit override)
#   2. <repo-root>/tab_quickstart.conf  (recommended; gitignored)
#   3. ~/.tab-quickstart.conf            (legacy fallback)
#
# Machine deployment:
#   single-machine (A=B same host): run all subcommands on the single GPU host
#   three-machine separated:        A=GPU bench, B=CPU orchestrator, C=LLM CLI host
# See tab_quickstart.sh help for per-subcommand "Runs on" target.
#
# All variables are bash-style KEY="value"; sourced before subcommand
# dispatch. Comments must start with '#'.

# === REQUIRED ===

# Shared / local working directory holding state, queue, results, logs.
# Single-machine mode: any writable local path.
# Three-machine mode: must be a real GPFS / NFS mount accessible from
# both the GPU host (A) and the orchestrator host (B).
TAB_GPFS_ROOT="/tmp/tab-shared"

# SSH target for the LLM CLI host. Format: user@host or a ~/.ssh/config
# alias. BatchMode key auth must work (no password prompts).
TAB_C_HOST="user@c-host"

# === TAB_C_CLI_CMD (REQUIRED) ===
#
# What it does:
#   The bench invokes the LLM CLI on the C host via SSH. For every LLM
#   request, the bench takes the prompt, runs shlex.quote() on it, then
#   substitutes it for the literal token '{prompt}' inside this template
#   to produce a fully resolved shell command. The bench then runs
#   `ssh <c-host> '<resolved command>'` and reads stdout as the reply.
#
# How to fill it:
#   - The template must contain the literal token '{prompt}' exactly once.
#   - Do NOT add quotes around '{prompt}' -- the bench wraps the actual
#     prompt with shlex.quote automatically. Manual quotes here would
#     deliver a quoted-string-as-prompt to the CLI.
#   - The template may contain shell variables (e.g. ${HOME}) or literal
#     JSON ({"k":"v"}); the bench uses plain .replace() and does not
#     parse the template with Python str.format.
#
# === Common CLI templates (pick the one that matches the CLI on C) ===
#
# Claude Code CLI (already logged in on C, using your Claude account quota):
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD='claude --print {prompt}'
#
# OpenAI Codex CLI (already logged in on C, using your Codex account quota):
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD='codex exec {prompt}'
#
# Any other CLI (anything that takes the prompt as part of argv and prints
# the reply on stdout):
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD='<your-cli> <subcommand> {prompt}'
#
# Advanced (change locale, add flags):
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD='env LANG=C claude --print --output-format text {prompt}'
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD='codex exec --json {prompt}'
#
# === Common mistakes (all are rejected at startup with rc=2) ===
#
# Wrong: quotes wrapped around the placeholder (CLI would see a quoted prompt)
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD='claude --print "{prompt}"'   # fatal: do NOT wrap
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD="codex exec '{prompt}'"       # fatal: do NOT wrap
#
# Wrong: placeholder missing
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD='claude --print'              # fatal: must contain {prompt}
#
# Wrong: placeholder repeated
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD='my-cli {prompt} {prompt}'    # fatal: exactly once
#
# Wrong: placeholder inside an outer quoted span
#   TAB_C_CLI_CMD='my-cli exec "prefix {prompt} suffix"'   # fatal: do NOT wrap

TAB_C_CLI_CMD='my-cli --print {prompt}'

# === OPTIONAL (have defaults) ===

# Bench repository root. Defaults to the git toplevel of the cwd at
# tab_quickstart.sh invocation.
# TAB_BENCH_REPO="/path/to/triton-ascend-bench"

# Resolver classification log (produced by 'resolve', consumed by
# 'smoke' / 'full').
# TAB_RESOLVE_LOG="$TAB_GPFS_ROOT/pa_resolve.log"

# Master triage state file path passed to run_acceptance_gate.sh.
# Per-phase state roots are always derived from TAB_GPFS_ROOT and are
# independent of this path.
# TAB_STATE_PATH="$TAB_GPFS_ROOT/state/triage_state.json"

# Per-call SSH/CLI transport timeout in seconds. Bump up for slow LLMs.
# TAB_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600

# Skip 'pip install -e .[automation,dev,gpu]' in 'setup' (use when deps
# are already verified to save several minutes).
# TAB_SETUP_SKIP_INSTALL=1

# Enable bash trace ('set -x') for debugging.
# TAB_VERBOSE=1
